                       T(r"**a.i.** Yes, Low for both: if the rival is High, Low gives 70 > 50; if Low, 30 > 10. **ii.** The unique Nash equilibrium is (Low, Low), payoffs (30, 30). **iii.** Both would earn more at (High, High) (50 each), but each has an incentive to undercut: individually rational choices give a collectively worse outcome, a prisoners' dilemma. In an indefinitely repeated game, trigger strategies (charge High until the rival undercuts, then Low for ever) can sustain (High, High) if the future is valued enough, since a one-off gain of 20 is outweighed by losing 20 in every later week ($\delta \geq 1/2$).",
                         r"**a.i.** 有，双方都是低价：对手高价时低价得 70 > 50；对手低价时得 30 > 10。**ii.** 唯一的纳什均衡是（低，低），收益 (30, 30)。**iii.** 双方在（高，高）都赚得更多（各 50），但都有压价的动机：个体理性的选择带来集体更差的结果，即囚徒困境。在无限重复博弈中，如果足够看重未来，触发策略（对手不压价就一直高价，一旦压价就永远低价）可以维持（高，高），因为一次性多赚的 20 抵不过之后每周少赚的 20（$\delta \geq 1/2$）。"),
                       T(r"**b.i.** [Tree.] By backward induction the incumbent accommodates (50 > 20), so the entrant enters (30 > 0): SPE (Enter, Accommodate), (30, 50). **ii.** Not credible: after entry fighting gives the incumbent 20 < 50, so it would not carry out the threat. **iii.** With the capacity, fighting gives 45 > 10, so the threat becomes credible; the entrant stays out (0 > −10) and the incumbent earns 60 > 50. It should invest: a credible commitment deters entry.",
                         r"**b.i.** [画树。] 逆向归纳：在位者接纳（50 > 20），所以进入者进入（30 > 0）：子博弈完美均衡（进入，接纳），(30, 50)。**ii.** 不可信：进入后开打只给在位者 20 < 50，它不会执行威胁。**iii.** 有了产能，开打得 45 > 10，威胁变得可信；进入者不进入（0 > −10），在位者得 60 > 50。应该投资：可信的承诺阻止了进入。"),
